{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat research/README.md reviews/2026-11-19/wp/phase1-axylo.report.md bench/size-latest.json'","aggregated_output":"# Axylo landscape research\n\nEvidence behind [docs/01-landscape.md](../docs/01-landscape.md). Collected 2026-11-17, with probes added and rerun on 2026-11-18 after review ([ledger](../reviews/2026-11-18/ledger.md)).\n\n## adoption/\n\n| File | What it is | How to refresh |\n|---|---|---|\n| `adoption.json` | npm weekly and yearly downloads, registry metadata, jsDelivr monthly hits and GitHub stars for about fifty charting packages | `node fetch.mjs > adoption.json && node refill.mjs` |\n| `httparchive.json` | Number of origins on which the HTTP Archive crawl detected each charting technology | `node httparchive.mjs > httparchive.json` |\n| `cadence.json` | Major-version dates and stable release counts for the ten studied libraries | `node cadence.mjs` |\n| `ranks.json` | Each candidate's rank on every adoption channel, and what each channel alone would select | `node ranks.mjs` |\n\nThe npm downloads API rate-limits bursts; `refill.mjs` retries the packages that came back empty.\n\n## harness/\n\nOne page runs the same tasks through the original ten libraries and Axylo. A probe drives system Chrome through all eleven.\n\nAxylo uses the production ES module from [`tests/dist/.packed/axylo-0.0.0.tgz`](../tests/dist/.packed/axylo-0.0.0.tgz), packed on 2026-11-18 at 21:10:31 UTC. The packing manifest records `sha512-LCn3nSF7J5rmBJmwBZbcAx6J2alUgEDGg6BQ44OmkziEpuzrFCX1qQ3CG9KMqgOAaPvKzh1LtfpRPM/FC2IfFQ==`. `node packed-axylo.mjs` checks that integrity and extracts the package into `vendor/axylo/`. Vite and the size script both resolve `axylo` to that copy.\n\nTo refresh from a new tarball, rerun `node packed-axylo.mjs` and record its filename, packing date and integrity here. A coordinator can repack an already-built distribution with `node scripts/pack.mjs --no-build` from the repository root. The harness needs its locked dependencies already installed. Preparing Axylo requires only the local archive.\n\n```bash\ncd research/harness\nnode packed-axylo.mjs\nnpx vite build\nnpx vite preview --port 4173 --strictPort   # leave running, then run below in another terminal\n```\n\n```bash\ncd research/harness\nnode probe.mjs                              # look, empty, a11y, env, perf\nnode probe.mjs dates sentinels lightonly    # added after review\nLIBS=highcharts-plain,echarts-aria node probe.mjs look a11y\nLIBS=noop,chartjs-tuned,echarts-tuned,recharts-tuned,highcharts-tuned,plotly-tuned node probe.mjs perf\nnode montage.mjs trend bars parts dirty empty kbd dark resize lightonly\nnode palette.mjs\nnode spot-checks.mjs\nnode sizes.mjs\ncd ../..\nnode research/tables.mjs\n```\n\n| Path | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `src/data.js` | The shared datasets. Every library receives exactly these values. |\n| `src/libs/<library>.js(x)` | The least configuration each library needs for each task. Comments mark what was required beyond data. |\n| `src/libs/<library>-tuned.js(x)` | The same large-data task in a tuned configuration. These change several options at once, some of them visible to the reader. |\n| `packed-axylo.mjs` | Verifies and unpacks the Axylo tarball for both bundle builds. |\n| `src/libs/highcharts-plain.js`, `echarts-aria.js` | Each library's accessibility switch in the other position. |\n| `src/libs/noop.js` | Draws nothing: the measurement floor. |\n| `probe.mjs` | DOM and accessibility-tree capture, keyboard walk, pointer hover in three time zones for instants and for date strings, one bad value at a time, resize, dark scheme, a light-only page on a dark device, motion with and without reduced-motion, timings and browser-reported main-thread time. |\n| `results.json` | Probe output, merged across runs. `_runs` lists every invocation since the log was added; results from the first pass predate it. |\n| `spot-checks.json` | Small checks the report quotes, including the WebGL renderer, reduced-motion mentions, accessibility switches, and what Axylo exposes after opening its table. |\n| `perf.log`, `rerun.log` | Console output of the first and second performance passes. The report uses the second. |\n| `shots/` | Screenshots; `_sheet-*.png` are the side-by-side sheets. |\n| `palette.json`, `sizes.json` | Default palette scores and bundle sizes. |\n\nOpen one case by hand at `http://localhost:4173/?lib=axylo&task=trend`. Tasks are `trend`, `dates`, `bars`, `parts`, `dirty`, `dirty-null`, `dirty-nan`, `dirty-string`, `dirty-undefined`, `empty`, `scale&n=100000`, `stream`. Add `&scheme=light` for a light-only page. Axylo simplifies dense lines by default and has no public rendering option for a tuned run. Its adapter uses the fixture's existing arrays in the documented column format.\n\n## palette/\n\n`node search.mjs` searches for 6- and 8-color categorical palettes that reach 3:1 contrast on light and dark backgrounds while staying apart under simulated color-vision deficiencies. `feasibility.json` holds the result. It shows which thresholds are reachable; it is not Axylo's palette.\n\n## tables.mjs\n\n`node tables.mjs` prints the Markdown tables in the landscape report from the JSON files above.\n\n### Reading the timings\n\nTimings are from headless Chrome on one desktop machine, three runs each, and are for ranking by order of magnitude. The report uses main-thread task time as the browser reports it (through the DevTools protocol), which counts work however a library schedules it but not rasterization on other threads. The older \"time to second frame\" figure is still recorded as `toPaintMs`; it cannot resolve below about 35 ms and stops counting before entry animations finish. The streaming producer sends one update per animation frame, so it is not an independent 60 Hz feed. WebGL ran on a software rasterizer. The performance plan replaces all of this with a stricter method ([docs/04-plan-performance.md](../docs/04-plan-performance.md)).\n<!-- Author: Codex, requested gpt-6.2-sol xhigh; observed gpt-6.2-sol, effort xhigh (session rollout turn_context). workspace-write. Reviewed by the coordinator (Claude Opus 5.5 high, cross-provider): the adapter and the probe hooks read for fairness. Saved by the coordinator. -->\n\nAxylo is wired into the Phase 1 harness alongside the original ten libraries. Vite and the size probe resolve `axylo` to the production ES module from `axylo-0.0.0.tgz`. The offline npm attempt returned `ENOTCACHED`, so `node packed-axylo.mjs` verifies the archive and unpacks it into `research/harness/vendor/axylo/`.\n\nThe tested archive was packed on 2026-11-18 at 21:10:31 UTC with integrity `sha512-LCn3nSF7J5rmBJmwBZbcAx6J2alUgEDGg6BQ44OmkziEpuzrFCX1qQ3CG9KMqgOAaPvKzh1LtfpRPM/FC2IfFQ==`. The refresh procedure is in the [research README](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/research/README.md).\n\n**Files changed.** Added `packed-axylo.mjs` and `src/libs/axylo.js`. Updated the harness `.gitignore`, `package.json`, `vite.config.js`, `src/main.js`, `probe.mjs`, `montage.mjs`, `palette.mjs`, `spot-checks.mjs`, and `sizes.mjs`, plus `research/README.md` and `research/tables.mjs`. The existing public API covers all tasks.\n\n### What each task needed beyond data\n\n| Task | Configuration |\n|---|---|\n| `trend` | Title, explicit instant axis for epoch milliseconds, and a channel field in long rows so the shared y axis can be titled “Sessions”. |\n| `dates` | Title and the same channel and y-axis bindings. Axylo infers calendar dates from the ISO strings. |\n| `bars` | Title, category and value bindings, and the supplied “Satisfied (%)” axis title. Baseline and label fitting use defaults. |\n| `parts` | Title, slice-label and value bindings, and the supplied “Share (%)” label. Legend and colors use defaults. |\n| `dirty` | Title and category and value bindings. All four sentinels pass through unchanged. |\n| `dirty-null` | Same bindings, with `null` passed through. |\n| `dirty-nan` | Same bindings, with `NaN` passed through. |\n| `dirty-string` | Same bindings, with `'40'` passed through as a string. |\n| `dirty-undefined` | Same bindings, with `undefined` passed through. |\n| `empty` | The trend configuration with zero rows and the built-in empty state. |\n| `scale` | Title, instant axis and value binding over the existing fixture arrays. Dense-line simplification is automatic, and Axylo exposes no public rendering switch for a tuned run. |\n| `stream` | The scale configuration plus `append(rows, { keep: 600 })`. |\n\nI treated the percent labels as fixture text and kept default number formatting. The Axylo-specific probes read plot labels from HTML, capture keyboard point text from `aria-valuetext`, retain the tooltip’s time zone, open the table before inspecting it, and read the rendered donut slice fills in order. The reduced-motion source check scans the unpacked package.\n\n### Verification\n\n`npx vite build` produced the Axylo chunk. The final lines were:\n\n```text\ndist/assets/echarts-DehbJkAK.js                       1,116.53 kB │ gzip:   370.42 kB\ndist/assets/plotly.min-V27pesPw.js                    4,651.94 kB │ gzip: 1,422.29 kB\n\n✓ built in 3.25s\n```\n\nThe size probe measured **105.9 KiB gzipped** for Axylo. All ten comparator rows matched a fresh run of the pre-change size script, although several values differ from the historical snapshot. Node checks verified fixture inputs for all 12 tasks, the expected packed-package diagnostics, and the 300 append calls with a 600-point window. `tables.mjs` printed the expected rows from a disposable copy with synthetic results. That copy was removed.\n\nChrome exited during startup with `setsockopt: Operation not permitted`. Browser measurements, screenshots, palette extraction, and the interactive spot checks are pending.\n\n### Coordinator rerun\n\nFrom the repository root, with the harness dependencies already installed:\n\n```bash\ncd research/harness\nnode packed-axylo.mjs\nnpx vite build\nnpx vite preview --port 4173 --strictPort\n```\n\nLeave preview running. In a second terminal, from the repository root:\n\n```bash\ncd research/harness\nnode probe.mjs\nnode probe.mjs dates sentinels lightonly\nLIBS=highcharts-plain,echarts-aria node probe.mjs look a11y\nLIBS=noop,chartjs-tuned,echarts-tuned,recharts-tuned,highcharts-tuned,plotly-tuned node probe.mjs perf\nnode montage.mjs trend bars parts dirty empty kbd dark resize lightonly\nnode palette.mjs\nnode spot-checks.mjs\nnode sizes.mjs\ncd ../..\nnode research/tables.mjs\n```{\n \"date\": \"2026-11-18T21:10:02.918Z\",\n \"method\": \"esbuild consumer bundles from tests/dist/fixtures (packed tarballs), minify, production condition; gzip level 9\",\n \"packed\": {\n  \"at\": \"2026-11-18T21:10:01.732Z\",\n  \"axylo\": \"sha512-LCn3nSF7J5rmBJmwBZbcAx6J2alUgEDGg6BQ44OmkziEpuzrFCX1qQ3CG9KMqgOAaPvKzh1LtfpRPM/FC2IfFQ==\",\n  \"commit\": \"208c56bea6a9c99d5480af709f84f83a7d86f77d\",\n  \"dirty\": false\n },\n \"cssFileBytes\": 14695,\n \"cssFileGzipBytes\": 3042,\n \"rows\": [\n  {\n   \"entry\": \"line only (examples/first-chart/npm.ts)\",\n   \"minBytes\": 280849,\n   \"jsGzipBytes\": 99135,\n   \"cssFileGzipBytes\": 0,\n   \"totalGzipBytes\": 99135,\n   \"totalKiB\": 96.81,\n   \"targetKiB\": 98,\n   \"targetBytes\": 100352,\n   \"over\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry\": \"everything (export * from axylo)\",\n   \"minBytes\": 334941,\n   \"jsGzipBytes\": 118522,\n   \"cssFileGzipBytes\": 0,\n   \"totalGzipBytes\": 118522,\n   \"totalKiB\": 115.74,\n   \"targetKiB\": 116,\n   \"targetBytes\": 118784,\n   \"over\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry\": \"area only (export { area } from axylo)\",\n   \"minBytes\": 286339,\n   \"jsGzipBytes\": 101091,\n   \"cssFileGzipBytes\": 0,\n   \"totalGzipBytes\": 101091,\n   \"totalKiB\": 98.72,\n   \"targetKiB\": null,\n   \"targetBytes\": null,\n   \"over\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry\": \"bar only (export { bar } from axylo)\",\n   \"minBytes\": 281874,\n   \"jsGzipBytes\": 99536,\n   \"cssFileGzipBytes\": 0,\n   \"totalGzipBytes\": 99536,\n   \"totalKiB\": 97.2,\n   \"targetKiB\": null,\n   \"targetBytes\": null,\n   \"over\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry\": \"scatter only (export { scatter } from axylo)\",\n   \"minBytes\": 267529,\n   \"jsGzipBytes\": 94737,\n   \"cssFileGzipBytes\": 0,\n   \"totalGzipBytes\": 94737,\n   \"totalKiB\": 92.52,\n   \"targetKiB\": null,\n   \"targetBytes\": null,\n   \"over\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry\": \"donut only (export { donut } from axylo)\",\n   \"minBytes\": 247371,\n   \"jsGzipBytes\": 86669,\n   \"cssFileGzipBytes\": 0,\n   \"totalGzipBytes\": 86669,\n   \"totalKiB\": 84.64,\n   \"targetKiB\": null,\n   \"targetBytes\": null,\n   \"over\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry\": \"validate only (export { validate } from axylo)\",\n   \"minBytes\": 58410,\n   \"jsGzipBytes\": 21053,\n   \"cssFileGzipBytes\": 0,\n   \"totalGzipBytes\": 21053,\n   \"totalKiB\": 20.56,\n   \"targetKiB\": null,\n   \"targetBytes\": null,\n   \"over\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry\": \"script tag (axylo.iife.min.js + axylo.css)\",\n   \"minBytes\": 335535,\n   \"jsGzipBytes\": 118680,\n   \"cssFileGzipBytes\": 3042,\n   \"totalGzipBytes\": 121722,\n   \"totalKiB\": 118.87,\n   \"targetKiB\": null,\n   \"targetBytes\": null,\n   \"over\": false\n  }\n ],\n \"breakdown\": {\n  \"rebuiltMinBytes\": 335044,\n  \"packedMinBytes\": 335044,\n  \"directories\": [\n   {\n    \"directory\": \"data\",\n    \"min B\": 74829,\n    \"share\": \"22.3%\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"directory\": \"dom\",\n    \"min B\": 58919,\n    \"share\": \"17.6%\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"directory\": \"core\",\n    \"min B\": 58302,\n    \"share\": \"17.4%\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"directory\": \"theme\",\n    \"min B\": 24618,\n    \"share\": \"7.3%\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"directory\": \"lookup\",\n    \"min B\": 21391,\n    \"share\": \"6.4%\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"directory\": \"render\",\n    \"min B\":